{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Mobile Price: the struck price, and the white band under checkout.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 1. THE STRUCK PRICE

  A cart line is a CSS grid with named areas. The price lives in `pr` and the
  quantity stepper in `qt`, immediately to its left.

  The price itself is .nc-lsave -- nc-linesave's element, NOT the theme's
  p.price, which is hidden on any line that has one. Its base rule is a flex
  ROW with white-space:nowrap, so the struck compare-at and the price charged
  sit side by side and refuse to wrap. There is a column override, but it does
  not reach a phone. So on a narrow drawer the pair is wider than its column,
  and because nowrap forbids breaking, it overflows LEFT -- straight under the
  + button. A struck number beside a quantity reads as a struck quantity.

  Stacking turns that overflow into height, which the row has to spare, and
  order:-1 lifts the struck figure ABOVE the price charged so it reads
  was-then-now down the column. Both .nc-lsave and p.price are covered, since
  which one renders depends on whether the line carries a saving.

  ---------------------------------------------------- 2. THE WHITE BAND

  The band under CHECKOUT is the sticky footer's own doing. position:sticky
  with bottom:0 pins an element to the bottom of the VIEWPORT only while its
  container is taller than the screen; when the cart is short, the element
  simply sits at its natural place in the flow and the rest of the panel's
  height stays empty below it. Padding was never the cause, which is why
  trimming padding did not shift it.

  So the pin is dropped on phones and the panel sits at the end of the content,
  where it ends when the content ends. A short cart no longer has a white band;
  a long cart scrolls to the button, which is one swipe on a list that short.

  Ordered after pg-cart-fast in footer-group, so this overrides the sticky rule
  it sets at equal specificity.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @media (max-width: 600px){
    /* ---- struck price above the price charged ---- */
    #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave,
    #cart .l4ca > li section .nc-lsave,
    #cart .l4ca > li .price,
    #cart .l4ca > li section .cols p.price{
      display:flex !important;
      flex-direction:column !important;
      align-items:flex-end !important;
      justify-content:flex-end !important;
      flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
      gap:1px !important;
      line-height:1.15 !important;
      text-align:right !important;
      max-width:100% !important;
      overflow:visible !important;
    }
    #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave s,
    #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave del,
    #cart .l4ca > li .price s,
    #cart .l4ca > li .price del{
      order:-1 !important;
      display:block !important;
      font-size:12px !important;
      font-weight:600 !important;
      line-height:1.15 !important;
      white-space:nowrap !important;
    }

    /* ---- no white band under the button ---- */
    #cart .sticky-in-panel{
      position:static !important;
      bottom:auto !important;
      padding-bottom:calc(4px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) !important;
      margin-bottom:0 !important;
    }
  }
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Mobile Price", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
